 For a drop-in, run the test from Pi Pocket's folder with the module copied in, or check it by hand: turn it on, ask Pi to use it in a session made for the purpose, and watch Menu → Extensions and the app's notices for errors.
 
+## Optional pi-agent-msgs slash integration
+
+The separately installed `pi-agent-msgs` drop-in may register `pi-agent-msgs.reporting-command`, a durable task with input `{ action: "on" | "off" | "status", by: ownerId }` and a result containing `reporting: boolean` (optional `message` and nullable `error`). Pocket’s owner-only `/agent-msgs` bridge invokes this fixed task for the current regular conversation without submitting model input. The drop-in must validate its owner, extension-enabled state, and receiver exclusion itself too. Its tool and task should use the same reporting-state function. Older drop-ins without this task receive an update error. No generic `registerCommand` API is added to drop-ins.
+
 ## A built-in extension
 
 A new file in `src/server/extensions/` is loaded into the running server about 300 ms after it is first saved, on, for everyone: there is no way to try it there first. So write it as a drop-in, check it on a copy ([self-editing.md](self-editing.md#check-it-on-a-copy)), and move it in when it works.
